==Finnish==

===Etymology===
A twentieth century invention usually interpreted as a variant of [[Saara]] ( =[[Sarah]]), rhyming with other popular 1960s names, [[Ari]], [[Jari]] and [[Mari]]. Other possible sources are Hungarian [[Sári]] ( a pet form of [[Sarah]]) and the place name [[Sariola]] in the [[Kalevala]] .

